2D integration methods of the semi-leptonic CC rates (GeneralEmAb).

All methods are stateless kernels (Opacity_CC_2D_<Method>_Nodes) that
take the Gauss-Legendre rules on [0,1] as arguments; Opacity_CC_2D (front
end ../wlSemiLeptonicOpacityModule2D.F90) calls them with the rules
computed once by InitOpacity_CC_2D (../wlSemiLeptonicNodes2D.F90). They
get all physics from
../wlSemiLeptonicPhysicsModule2D.F90; they differ only in the quadrature.
The method is chosen by InitOpacity_CC_2D(nE, Method_Option); without
Method_Option it is the compile-time default, make
EMAB2D_METHOD=MOMENTUM|ENERGY|TAIL (default MOMENTUM).

  wlSemiLeptonicIntegration2D_Energy.F90      ENERGY, the "STANDARD" method
      Linear Gauss-Legendre in the nucleon energy E2 (outer) and lepton
      energy E3 (inner), nE x nE nodes: the layout of the original GSI
      routines (../OriginalGSIroutines). Opacity_CC_2D_Energy_Nodes
      (independent E2 and E3 rules; Init uses gauleg(nE) for both). Kinks and
      SQRT endpoints of the integrand are not resolved, so it converges
      slowly (~n^-3).

  wlSemiLeptonicIntegration2D_Momentum.F90    MOMENTUM, the DEFAULT method
      Outer integral in the nucleon momentum p2, split at the two-body
      thresholds of the lepton window and at the nucleon-2 Fermi edge
      (P2_Segments); inner integral in the lepton momentum p3, split at the
      kinks of the angle-integrated |M|^2 and at the lepton and nucleon-4
      Fermi edges, with a quadratic map at the end where nucleon 4 is at
      rest (E3_Segments_Fermi, E3_Node). Without the Fermi-edge splits the
      method converged to wrong values for T <~ 5 MeV (e.g. +25% for
      electron captures at T = 2.4 MeV even at nE = 96). nE nodes per outer
      segment, Inner_Rule(nE) = MAX(8,MIN(12,nE/2)) nodes per inner
      segment. Thermal cutoff Tfac = 30 above the kinematic threshold.
      Opacity_CC_2D_Momentum_Nodes (explicit outer and inner rules, inner
      1..12 nodes, otherwise it returns 0; Init uses gauleg(nE) and
      Inner_Rule(nE)).

  wlSemiLeptonicIntegration2D_Tail.F90        TAIL
      Kink- and Fermi-edge-split finite segments with endpoint clustering
      plus a 12-point Gauss-Laguerre tail (scale T) instead of a thermal
      cutoff. Most accurate (corrections 0-2 ~1e-6 at nE = 12); used as the
      reference in the comparison tests. Opacity_CC_2D_Tail_Nodes
      (Init uses gauleg(nE)).

  wlSemiLeptonicOpacityIntegrationModule2D.F90
      Two-phase (GPU-oriented) driver of the MOMENTUM method
      (CC2D_PrepareCall / CC2D_SetInnerRule / CC2D_RowSetup(CD, iE2, RD) /
      CC2D_NodeKernel / CC2D_ApplyPrefactor and per-reaction wrappers),
      reading the rules of InitOpacity_CC_2D; bit-identical to
      Opacity_CC_2D with the MOMENTUM method.

MOMENTUM, max pointwise rel. error (corrections 0-2, e and mu, reactions
1-4, 1-300 MeV, samples with kappa >= 1e-10 cm^-1; emissivity where the
inverse-decay kappa >= 1e-10 cm^-1). Reference TAIL nE = 24 on every 5th
row of ThermoConditions.dat, ENERGY 768x768 for the low-T set (40 rows with
T scaled by 0.5, 0.25, 0.1, T >= 1 MeV). Serial us/eval (gfortran -O2).
  nE (inner)   ThermoCond.  low T r1-3  low T r4   us/eval
  12 (8)       4.5e-3       2.7e-2      1.0e-1     26
  16 (8)       4.3e-4       4.2e-3      5.6e-2     35
  20 (10)      1.0e-4       1.3e-3      2.5e-2     52
  24 (12)      5.0e-5       6.0e-4      4.2e-3     77
  32 (12)      5.0e-5       5.9e-4      1.2e-3     97
For comparison (same cost measure): GSI code at Ngrids = 50, 158 us, ~2.7e-3
on reactions 1-2 and unusable for 3-4; ENERGY 50x50, 162 us, ~1.6e-3;
TAIL nE = 6, 111 us, ~4.4e-4. The low-T emissivity errors are at E ~ 1 MeV
and T < 2 MeV. Correction 3 (form factors) is limited to a few % above
~150 MeV in every method by the discontinuous form-factor term.
